OL,3,GNEWSAReduced rail service continues due
OL,4,Ato dry weather
OL,5,
OL,6,FA rail operator has confirmed its
OL,7,Freduced timetable will remain in place
OL,8,Fbecause of the dry weather.
OL,10,FSouth Western Railway (SWR) and Network
OL,11,FRail Wessex said the service between
OL,12,FExeter St Davids and London Waterloo
OL,13,Fwould remain two-hourly and speed
OL,14,Frestrictions would continue until there
OL,15,Fwas "significant rainfall".
OL,17,FThe Salisbury to Exeter Rail User Group
OL,18,F(SERUG) has described the early morning
OL,19,Ftimetable as "unacceptable" for
OL,20,Fcommuters in east Devon.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
